  "name": null,
  "problem": "Using the data from part $5,$ find an **exact** equation of the line for the distance $d$ covered by Sam after $t$ minutes.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $d=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $d$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $d$-axis at the origin. So, the $d$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(11,300),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{d}_{2}-{d}_{1}}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{300-0}{11-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{300}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\frac{300}{11}$ and the $d$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept form $d=mt+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\nd=\\frac{300}{11}t\n$$",
